Third-party material

The files in src/classdefs, and the copies of them that the build embeds in the XAR, are definitions
of XWiki's own classes (XWiki.UIExtensionClass, XWiki.ConfigurableClass, XWiki.SchedulerJobClass,
XWiki.Mail and others). They were extracted from XWiki 17.10 with tools/extract_classdef.py, with
whitespace normalised. They are embedded because an XAR carries the class definition of every object
in it, as XWiki's own exports do, so the import does not depend on what the target wiki has. A stub
definition (property names without their types) made an import fail on 17.10 with "string data, right
truncation; size limit: 768", because XWiki then stored long text properties as short strings. Leaving
the definitions out altogether also imported cleanly on 17.10.14 (checked 14 Nov 2026), because that
wiki already had XWiki's own classes.

They remain the work of the XWiki contributors. XWiki states on https://www.xwiki.org/xwiki/bin/view/Main/License
that its code is under the GNU LGPL 2.1 and that its default wiki documents are under Creative Commons
Attribution (CC-BY), copyright "XWiki" (the XWiki open source project). Credit is given here for that
reason. Nothing else in this repository is copied from XWiki.
